=== COMPILER2 DIAGNOSTICS ===
  [hir] E0010

  × `client<llm>` config blocks are removed; declare a client value instead: `client LegacyOpenAI = openai.OpenAiClient.new(model = "...");` (compose reliability with ai.Retry / ai.Fallback /
  │ ai.RoundRobin)
    ╭─[client_option_types.baml:9:1]
  9 │ ╭─▶ client<llm> LegacyOpenAI {
 10 │ │       provider openai
 11 │ │       options {
 12 │ │           model "gpt-4"
 13 │ │           max_tokens 100
 14 │ │           temperature 0.7
 15 │ │           base_url "https://api.openai.com/v1"
 16 │ │       }
 17 │ ├─▶ }
    · ╰──── replace with `client Name = <expr>;`
    ╰────

  [hir] E0010

  × `retry_policy` blocks are removed; wrap the client instead: `client Reliable = ai.Retry.new(<inner>, max_attempts = ...);` (`LegacyRetry` has no effect)
    ╭─[client_option_types.baml:20:1]
 20 │ ╭─▶ retry_policy LegacyRetry {
 21 │ │       max_retries 3
 22 │ ├─▶ }
    · ╰──── retry composes at the client boundary now
    ╰────

  [hir] E0010

  × LLM function `UnknownProviderPrefix` has an unusable `client`: no builtin provider for prefix "aws-bedrock"; construct a client value instead (OpenAI-compatible endpoints:
  │ openai.OpenAiClient.new(base_url = ..., model = "anthropic.claude-3-haiku"))
    ╭─[client_option_types.baml:38:57]
 38 │ ╭─▶ function UnknownProviderPrefix(input: string) -> string {
 39 │ │       client: "aws-bedrock/anthropic.claude-3-haiku"
 40 │ │       prompt: `${input}`
 41 │ ├─▶ }
    · ╰──── use a "provider/model" string or an expression evaluating to ai.Client
    ╰────
